input:
Evaluate \begin{align*}
\left(c^c-c(c-1)^c\right)^c
\end{align*} when $c=3$.

output:
The expected value is the sum of the products of each outcome and its probability.
In this case, the expected value is $\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)(3) + \left(\frac{2}{3}\right)(-2) = \frac{1}{3}(3) - \frac{2}{3}(2) = \frac{1}{3} - \frac{4}{3} = \boxed{-\frac{1}{3}}$.
The answer is: -\frac{1}{3}

